Original commit body from 501cc63:

Binary files (images, audio, video, fonts, archives, PDFs) cannot be
meaningfully embedded for semantic similarity. This change adds these
file extensions to ADDITIONAL_FILES_EXCLUDES to avoid wasting compute
on files that won't produce useful results.

File types now excluded:
- Images: png, jpg, jpeg, gif, svg, ico, webp, bmp, tiff, tif, psd
- Audio/video: mp3, wav, ogg, flac, m4a, aac, mp4, webm, avi, mov, mkv
- Fonts: ttf, woff, woff2, eot, otf
- Archives: zip, tar, gz, tgz, rar, 7z, bz2, xz
- Binary data: bin, dat, npy, npz, pkl, pickle
- Documents: pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx

This significantly reduces the number of files to embed in repos with
media assets (e.g., litellm went from 1628 to ~800 Additional Files).
